      "title": "Career Services",
      "description": "Career Services - Davis & Elkins College Skip to the content Davis & Elkins College Search: Search Search Academics Academics Overview Calendar Majors & Programs Pre-Professional Studies Course Catalog Directory Educational Support Booth Library Career Services Life at D&E Life at D&E Overview Residential Life Dining Services Health & Safety Morrison-Novakovic Center for Faith and Public Policy Clubs & Organizations Bookstore Admissions Admission Overview Apply Request Info Contact Us Tuition & Aid Tuition & Aid Overview Tuition Costs Financial Aid Scholarships Athletics Calendar About D&E About D&E Overview Office of the President Leadership Mission, Vision & History Directory Campus Map Explore Elkins Ministry Connections Work at D&E The Senator Daily My D&E Alumni Give Back Graduates of the Last Decade (GOLD) Administrative Requests Calendar Merch & Perks Alumni Association Board Spotlight Stories Chapters Forward Magazine Current Students Self-Service Portal Forms, Tools & Resources Student Billing Registrar Course Catalog Bookstore Booth Library Career Services Commencement New & Prospective Students Enroll Visit Virtual Tour Tuition & Aid International Students Transfer Students Important Forms For Parents & Families Faculty/Staff Self-Service Portal Informer Visit Give Request Info Info Apply Home > Academics > Career Services Career Services Take the next step in your journey. As a student’s time at D&E ends, the Office of Career Services is here to help ensure a smooth transition. Whether their next move is to launch their career or enter graduate school, we offer resources and guidance to fuel their success. Career Services aims to equip and empower graduating students to effectively advance their professional development as they build thriving careers and healthy lives committed to impactful local and world citizenship. We also work with D&E alumni . The Career Services Pathway The Career Services Pathway captures how Career Services empowers the D&E community to develop to their full potential and enhance their personal excellence and professional marketability. Let’s Begin the Journey KNOW KNOW Strategic career guidance, helping students understand their own individual interests, preferences, passions, strengths, and values as they relate to professional development Strategic career guidance, helping students understand their own individual interests, preferences, passions, strengths, and values as they relate to professional development EXPLORE EXPLORE Supports students in developing a knowledge base of potential professional and career next steps Supports students in developing a knowledge base of potential professional and career next steps PREPARE PREPARE Provides students with practical aid in developing the tools and skills necessary for achieving the next career step, including effective online profiles, résumés and cover letters, successful internship experiences, positive interviews, and networking opportunities Provides students with practical aid in developing the tools and skills necessary for achieving the next career step, including effective online profiles, résumés and cover letters, successful internship experiences, positive interviews, and networking opportunities LAUNCH LAUNCH Assists graduating students as they begin life after graduation in whatever professional steps they take, including identifying opportunities for them to connect with employers worldwide. Assists graduating students as they begin life after graduation in whatever professional steps they take, including identifying opportunities for them to connect with employers worldwide. Internship Opportunities We’ve got everything to get you started with an internship. Quick Start Guide Quick Start Guide Access the guide Step-by-Step Instructions Step-by-Step Instructions Access the Video Setup Tutorial Internship Portal Internship Portal Access the Portal Principles & Disclaimers Career Services abides by the principles established by the following professional associations: NACE, NCDA, ACA, and NSEA. Disclaimer: Career Services makes no representations or guarantees about positions listed on its website and is not responsible for the safety, wages, working conditions, or other aspects of employment. It is the responsibility of the student or alumnus to take all necessary precautions when interviewing for or accepting any position. He or she is solely responsible for obtaining or confirming any necessary information concerning an employer. The Career Services website also contains links to other websites as a convenience for its users and is not responsible for the contents of any linked site. Anyone who discovers misuse or abuse of our website is encouraged to report the matter to Career Services, either in person or via careerservices@dewv.edu . Career Services Justin Bowers Director, Career Services Email Justin Bowers 304-637-1220 Jennings Randolph Hall 100 Campus Drive, Elkins, W.Va. 26241 304-637-1900 100 Campus Drive Elkins, W.Va. 26241 304-637-1900 Contact Us Instagram Tik Tok X YouTube Flickr Facebook LinkedIn Upcoming  Events Full Calendar 9/18 D&E Day of Service All day 9/25 Homecoming 2026 All day 10/1 Fall Break (No Classes) All day 11/7 Admission Open House 8 am.–1 pm. Myles Center for the Arts Myles Center for the Arts Full Calendar Explore D&E Campus Map Booth Library Flynn Planetarium Graceland Inn Bookstore Employment Contact Us Tools & Resources Transcript Request Password Reset Media Kit My D&E Portal Directory Compliance & Administration Consumer Information Title IX & Discrimination and Harassment ©2026 Davis & Elkins College  |  All Rights Reserved Explore D&E Search: Search"
